  "body": "### Summary\nThe poll answer ⊖ touch-target test should prove that the glyph stays centred in its 44 pt button. A one-sided overhang would otherwise slip through.\n\n### Scope\n- `ComposerTouchTargetTests` (#1307) checks the button's laid-out size and overhang, not where the glyph sits.\n- Mutation it misses: `PollCreationSheet.swift:166` `.padding(.horizontal, -overhang)` → `.padding(.leading, -2 * overhang)`. The ⊖ moves 13.7 pt onto the answer field (xSmall), and every case stays green.\n- Fix: probe the glyph's global frame inside the hosted button, and assert that its centre equals the layout's centre on both axes.\n\n### Blocked by\n#1307\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The one-sided mutation fails the test, and the five Dynamic Type cases stay green on the real code.\n\nFound by the adversarial review of #1307 (Opus 5.5, r1307).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
